  "summary": "Painted rafter patterns in Māori meeting houses featuring flowing geometric designs based on natural forms and ancestral stories.",
  "description": "Characterized by flowing, rhythmic patterns of spirals (koru), crescents (kape), and zigzags (rautupiri) painted in red, black, and white on wooden rafters. Developed as a visual language to complement whakairo carving, representing tribal identity, genealogical connections, and natural elements.",
